  "description": "An ensemble of classical models (scikit-learn) that predicts a number from 8 numeric features (e.g. house prices): gradient boosting, a support vector machine and a Gaussian process with an RBF + noise kernel, combined by stacking. A ridge regression learns from their predictions for rows they were not fitted on (5-fold cross-validation) how to weigh them. The dotted connections into the stacking brick carry the models themselves.",
